## 7. Theorem

**Full Graph-Incidence Tangent and Normal Decomposition Theorem.** On the
selected eta9 residue carrier, the three-graph incidence map has rank 126 and
kernel rank 123. The selected member and the 33 principal directions span a
rank-34 subspace of that kernel. A canonical exact extension supplies 89
additional graph-preserving directions, so the projective graph-preserving
tangent has rank 122 and the true incidence-normal quotient has rank 126. The
old rank-215 quotient by the principal slice is an extension of the rank-126
normal quotient by the omitted rank-89 tangent sector.

**Proof.** The packet reconstructs the hash-locked G3AG matrix over the
selected degree-six residue field and computes its rank and canonical kernel.
It independently rebuilds `s_union`, embeds all 33 principal columns in the
249-coordinate basis, and verifies that the matrix kills them and the selected
member. Exact row reduction extends these 34 vectors by 89 canonical kernel
vectors to a basis of `K`. Adding the 126 pivot-coordinate complement vectors
then gives a full rank-249 frame. The displayed exact sequences and dimensions
follow. QED.

